# Build context hygiene for Dockerfile.seed.
#
# CI publishes this image from a clean checkout, so it only ever sees tracked
# files. A LOCAL build (docker-compose.oss.yml `connector-seed`) uses the working
# tree instead, and the seed is `cp -a`'d onto the mcp_connectors volume — so
# anything stray here lands on a self-hoster's connector tree. Measured on a
# developer tree: 87.5MB seeded instead of 25.4MB, of which 51.5MB was a stray
# python3.11 venv and 29MB was 1224 stale .pyc files.
#
# The .pyc are the part that actually bites: connectors are patched in place
# (see CLAUDE.md "patch the active version in place"), and CPython validates
# cached bytecode on (source mtime-seconds, source size). A baked .pyc that
# collides on both against a patched .py runs the OLD connector silently.
#
# Keeping this list aligned with .gitignore is what makes a local build produce
# the same artifact CI publishes.

# Stale bytecode — must never reach the volume.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]

# Developer virtualenvs (gitignored; pinned to a host interpreter, useless in-image).
**/venv/
**/.venv/
**/env/

# Not runtime artifacts.
**/tests/
**/test_*.py
**/*_test.py
**/.pytest_cache/
**/*.md
**/.DS_Store

# The generation moat is already excluded by Dockerfile.seed's allowlist COPY;
# listed here too so a future COPY . never silently reintroduces it.
generators/
oauth/
